  "post": {
    "caption": "Morganite is named after a banker. Tiffany's gemologist George Kunz chose the name to honor banker and gem collector John Pierpont Morgan, and much of Morgan's gem collection went to a New York museum. Its first stones were found in Madagascar around 1910, and many morganites are heated to give a purer pink. Morganite is a pink variety of beryl.",
